# The module label, and only the module label.
#
# Frappe v16 reads translations from a compiled catalogue
# (`sites/assets/locale/<lang>/LC_MESSAGES/<app>.mo`) and never from `translations/*.csv`;
# `bench build --app smartprocess_logistics` and `bench compile-translations` build that
# catalogue from the `.po` files in this directory. An app whose catalogue carries a msgid
# shared with ERPNext would translate it for every screen in the language, so this file
# deliberately holds one entry: the name the Desk shows for this module.
